:''This article is about the Cat Unit. For the enemy, see [[Gudebene Cat (Enemy)]].
'''Gudetama Cat''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] introduced in [[Version 6.2 Update|Version 6.2]] and was created by a [[Gudetama Collaboration Event|collaboration]] between Battle Cats and Sanrio's Gudetama. This character can be unlocked by logging into the game during the collab. [[True Form]] added in [[Version 7.1 Update|Version 7.1]] gains [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]] and increases its health.

{{Cat Info
|ID = 347
|rarity = EX
|name1 = Gudetama Cat
|name2 = Gude Omelette Cat
|name3 = Gudebene Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Gude Omelette Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Gudebene Cat''' when obtained from [[Gudetama Cat Awakens!]] (may be dropped on the first stage but guaranteed on the second stage) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
This Gudetama-carrying-cat is practically worthless outside of its [[True Form]], as it is way too pricey and is outclassed by so many other options, like [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Fish Cat]].

==='''True Form'''===
In its [[True Form]], it can be used as an excellent [[Immune to Waves|anti-wave]] meatshield. However, once they are unlocked, [[Gold Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Glittering Macho Cat]], or a [[Talents|Talented]] [[Li'l Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Mohawk Cat]] are much more effective alternatives due to their cheaper price. Unlike the previous cats though, its Strong ability allows it to survive a hit from [[Berserkory]], [[Two Can]] and [[Infernal Pegasus Deonil]], but there will usually be supporting enemies or peons to kill Gudebene anyways. If this cat is used though, the wallet must be watched closely because of its high price.

To put it short, this cat was incredible relative to how easy it is to obtain, but it has been overshadowed by even better cats in the years since its release.

{{Job|Classification = Meatshield}}

